  "key_concepts": [
    "LSystem SOP rewrites strings through generations and interprets the result as turtle-style geometry.",
    "Output can be skeleton or tube, and tube-specific controls only matter for tube output.",
    "Non-integer generations use continuous angle, length, and width controls for smooth animation.",
    "Rules can use context, conditions, probability, and explicit variables, but official rule-length/nesting/count limits still apply.",
    "J/K/M source inputs support stamped/copy geometry in advanced rule workflows."
